# Citation metadata for GitHub ("Cite this repository") and Zenodo.
# Update version and date-released at each release. After the first Zenodo
# archive, add the concept DOI under "identifiers".
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WeGrowHealthR, please cite it as below, together with the studies whose methods you use (see wgh_references())."
type: software
title: "WeGrowHealthR: Child Growth Data Analysis, Modelling and Reproducible Research Workflows"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: GPL-3.0-only
authors:
  - family-names: Ho
    given-names: Nhan Thi
    email: nhanhocumc@gmail.com
keywords:
  - child growth
  - anthropometry
  - growth references
  - SITAR
  - quantile regression
  - reproducible research
  - R
abstract: >-
  Tools and one-call workflows for longitudinal child growth data, written to
  accompany the books Child Growth Data Analysis and Modeling with R and its
  advanced companion. The package covers data cleaning, WHO and CDC z-scores
  and nutritional status, prevalence and trends, mixed-model trajectories,
  SITAR growth curves, quantile regression and linear quantile mixed models,
  conditional growth references, functional phenotypes, multistate models,
  prediction benchmarks with SHAP explanations, reproducible parallel
  computing and a simulation engine for teaching cohorts with known truth.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Overweight and obesity epidemic, temporal trends and regional disparities in physical growth of Vietnamese children"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ho
        given-names: Nhan Thi
      - family-names: Bangsberg
        given-names: David
      - family-names: Hermiston
        given-names: Michelle L
    journal: "Scientific Reports"
    volume: 16
    start: 7515
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1038/s41598-026-37210-w
